=== soak.sh — translation verdict, taken before anything is run ===
  uname machine        : aarch64
  process architecture : arm64 (ELF e_machine of /proc/self/exe)
  /proc/cpuinfo        : CPU implementer 0x61 (arm-shaped)
  /run/rosetta         : absent
  binfmt_misc for self : no interpreter registered that would run arm64
  verdict              : NATIVE — kernel and process agree on aarch64, /proc/cpuinfo is consistent with arm64, no Rosetta marker, no matching binfmt_misc interpreter.

soak: REFUSING a reproduction leg against 'head'.
  HEAD f3b68f5

  A reproduction leg exists to show the harness can SEE the defect, so it has to run a
  binding that still HAS it: one at or before 7f6a936^, the commit
  before every crossing moved onto binding-owned engine threads. 'head' is not an
  ancestor of it.

  This is refused rather than warned about because it is the front door to the exact
  inference this tool exists to refuse: a post-fix binding that died for any reason at
  all would write REPRODUCED to the ledger, and every later soak on this architecture
  would then read VALIDATED.
